/**
 * The shape LIBRARY — every stampable glyph that is data rather than JSX.
 *
 * The original catalogue is 214 shapes hand-written as JSX in the canvas
 * renderer, one `{shapeType === 'x' && (<svg>…)}` block each. That is a fine
 * way to draw twenty shapes and an impossible way to draw two thousand, so
 * everything here is DATA: one row per shape, rendered by a single branch in
 * the renderer and by the same code in the picker preview.
 *
 * Two sources, one format:
 *   • Lucide (lucide-static, ISC licence) — 1776 named things, carrying Lucide's
 *     own search keywords. Line art, so these draw stroke-only.
 *   • Generated geometry — polygons, stars, bursts, gears, arrows, callouts,
 *     banners, frames and flowchart symbols, 227 of them. Closed paths, so
 *     these take the object's fill like the original catalogue does.
 *
 * Nodes use a compact DSL rather than JSON: at this many shapes the JSON
 * punctuation alone would be tens of kilobytes of bundle for nothing.
 *
 *   p<d>                        path
 *   c<cx>,<cy>,<r>              circle
 *   r<x>,<y>,<w>,<h>,<rx>,<ry>  rect
 *   l<x1>,<y1>,<x2>,<y2>        line
 *   e<cx>,<cy>,<rx>,<ry>        ellipse
 *   y<points> / g<points>       polyline / polygon
 *
 * joined with '~', which never occurs in SVG path data. Everything is drawn in
 * a 24x24 viewBox.
 *
 * GENERATED — do not hand-edit. Lucide is ISC; its notice is in the repo and
 * the attribution belongs in the app's credits alongside Icons8's.
 */

